# What does NOT belong in the repo, and why.
#
# The rule: source and fitted parameters are committed; anything that is a cache of
# somebody else's API, or a bulk intermediate the pipeline rebuilds from one, is not.
# The whole build is 552 MB and 343 MB of that is cache.

# --- API and scrape caches (regenerable, need a CFBD key) --------------------
cfbd_cache/
cfbd_cache_gt/
ourlads_cache/
twodeep_cache/

# --- bulk intermediates ------------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is rebuilt by the stage above it, and each is 4-48 MB. The
# per-facet frames are the worst: hybrid_player_war_by_facet.csv alone is 48 MB and
# is just hybrid_player_war.csv before the facets are summed away.
*.parquet
*.npy
hybrid_player_war_by_facet.csv
player_war_by_facet.csv
player_war_uncertainty.csv
player_projection_uncertainty.csv
horse_race_matrix.csv
candidate_team_totals.csv
candidate_team_z.csv

# --- raw pulls ---------------------------------------------------------------
roster_2025.json
games_2025.json
portal_2026.json
rec_*.json
report.json
report_2026.json

# --- generated reports (the site publishes its own) --------------------------
war_2026.html
war_diagnostics.html

# --- environments ------------------------------------------------------------
rbenv/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# --- superseded by the hybrid build -----------------------------------------
# build_war.py's PFF-only artifacts and the v1 projection. Nothing downstream reads
# them - src/data/war.py takes hybrid_player_war.csv and projections_2026_v2.csv - and
# they are 6.5 MB of player rows kept only as a record of a build that was replaced.
player_war.csv
projections_2026.csv
rb_all.csv
rb_career.csv
rb_qualified.csv
roster_2026_features.csv
team_facet_totals.csv
team_facet_z.csv
team_ratings.csv
